# nsMsgProgress::OnProgressChange behavior in mailnews/base/src/nsMsgProgress.cpp

Forwards all six arguments to each live weak listener and removes dead entries. Progress amounts are not cached, so later registration does not replay numeric progress. Dynamic forward iteration follows the same Gecko array rules as OnStateChange.

## State read

- mListenerInfoList; all progress arguments

## State changed

- Dead entries removed; no numeric progress cache

## Calls and triggers

- OnProgress adapts 64-bit input and calls this at226-229.
- Compose UI listener uses total current/max to set meter percent and taskbar; max>65536 triggers determinate taskbar updates at988-1005.

## Result and consumers

NS_OK after callback loop; callback results ignored.

## Errors

Dead listeners silently removed.

## Async completion

Synchronous relay; no completion promise.

## Ownership and cleanup

Temporary strong referent for callback duration only.

